---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const sections = [
  { id: 'the-short-version', label: 'The short version' },
  { id: 'amazon-associates', label: 'Amazon Associates' },
  { id: 'how-i-pick-products', label: 'How I pick products' },
  { id: 'no-paid-placements', label: 'No paid placements' },
  { id: 'prices', label: 'Prices' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  description="How affiliate links work on Eidolon, how products are picked, and what I never do."
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="the-short-version">The short version</h2>
  <p>
    Some articles on this site — mostly the ones comparing products like protein powders or
    supplements — contain affiliate links. I earn a commission if you buy through these links, at no
    extra cost to you. The price you pay is the same whether you use my link or go to the site
    directly.
  </p>

  <h2 id="amazon-associates">Amazon Associates</h2>
  <p>
    As an Amazon Associate, I earn from qualifying purchases made through links to Amazon on this
    site.
  </p>

  <h2 id="how-i-pick-products">How I pick products</h2>
  <p>
    I don't pick a product just because it pays the highest commission. Before I recommend anything,
    I check:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Whether it's been tested by an independent, third-party lab</li>
    <li>Whether the brand holds a valid FSSAI licence</li>
    <li>
      What's actually in it — the ingredient list and quantities, not just the marketing claims
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    This follows the Advertising Standards Council of India's (ASCI) guidelines for influencer
    advertising — if a post contains an affiliate link, it's labelled, on the page and here.
  </p>

  <h2 id="no-paid-placements">No paid placements</h2>
  <p>
    I don't run paid product placements without a clear label. If a brand ever pays for a mention,
    that post will say so plainly — the same ASCI guidelines apply to that as they do to affiliate
    links.
  </p>

  <h2 id="prices">Prices</h2>
  <p>
    Product pages on this site don't show prices, because they change often and I'd rather send you
    to the retailer's page for the current price than show you something out of date.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
